--
-- Archaeology (world): Draenor / Broken Isles / Kul Tiras / Zandalar dig sites.
-- Companion update to arch_world_db_tables.sql: adds every ResearchSite row of
-- build 12.1.0.69814 that the consolidated file does not carry (its content
-- stops at Pandaria, map 870).
--
--   * 177 sites: 54 on Draenor (1116), 76 on the Broken Isles (1220),
--     23 on Zandalar (1642), 24 on Kul Tiras (1643).
--   * polygons: 12 vertices each, joined ResearchSite.QuestPOIBlobID ->
--     QuestPOIPoint (12.1.0.69814 client export), ordered by QuestPOIPoint ID.
--   * branch mapping: warcraft.wiki.gg / wowpedia "Dig site" tables for 150
--     sites (marked plain). The remaining 27 are PROVISIONAL zone/name
--     inference and are marked inline with their reasoning - confirm against
--     live data (e.g. the HandyNotes: Archaeology addon database) before
--     trusting them for gameplay.
--
-- Deliberately NOT inserted (still present in ResearchSite.db2):
--   140/142/161/949/951  dev "TEMPLATE" placeholders (no polygon at all)
--   1784                 "PH West Talador Dig Site (disabled)" placeholder
--   2115/2117/2118       Southern Barrens warfront phase POIs (icon 0)
--   471/473/475          Vashj'ir dig sites (Night Elf) - removed from the
--                        game; re-add with branch 4 if underwater sites are
--                        wanted and their polygons are still valid
-- Same-name site pairs (Timeworn Strand 1935/1976, Meredil 2033/2039, Crimson
-- Thicket 2035/2045) are distinct polygons, both kept.
--
-- ACTIVATION NOTE: these rows load the site reference data; the branch
-- wiring that makes the sites surveyable (find GameObjects + loot) ships in
-- the companion file arch_world_find_objects_draenor_legion_bfa.sql.
-- Safe to re-run: the DELETEs only clear the ids this file re-inserts.
--


